# ANTONYM facts sample (ConceptNet /r/Antonym / WordNet export format, one pair per line "a b", symmetric, a<->b)
#
# **ANTONYM ~ EDGE_SIMILAR symmetric shape, distinct from SIMILAR semantics**:
#   - SIMILAR = similar (big ~ tall, X like Y) -> similar_facts / EDGE_SIMILAR
#   - ANTONYM = opposite (big <-> small, hot <-> cold, concept<->concept 1st-order) -> this file
#   **not verify_inverse**: algebraic inverse = transform<->transform (d/dx<->int, +<->-, T-L4,
#   verify_inverse verifies B.compose(A)=identity, math transforms only); language antonym =
#   concept<->concept (verify_inverse returns None can't-verify for word pairs, #479 external seed).
#
# **symmetric storage**: unordered symmetric pair (a<->b, once per pair, canonical order a<=b),
# bootstrap_antonym_edges builds single edge a->b; reader (pending wiring, mirrors similar_candidates
# out_edges+in_edges bidirectional query) yields a<->b closure. Unlike alias explicit bidirectional.
#
# **not core data** (iron law "no hardcode", same as antonym_facts_zh.txt.sample):
#   - core code (pure_integer_ai/ package) never imports this file, core does not know pair contents,
#     loader (collection.resolve_antonym_facts) is pluggable data ingestion; production default has no
#     this file (PURE_INTEGER_AI_LOCAL_DIR unset/file absent) -> resolve returns [] -> boot zero side effects
#     -> bit-identical.
#   - antonym facts file is external antonym pairs (ConceptNet/WordNet objective assertions,
#     source (1) EPI_STRUCTURED, not system teacher judgment, #479).
#
# Usage: user exports ConceptNet /r/Antonym or WordNet antonym to this format,
# place at $PURE_INTEGER_AI_LOCAL_DIR/antonym_facts_en.txt.
# formal_train boot reads this -> bootstrap_antonym_edges builds EDGE_ANTONYM (a->b single,
# static strength=1, not reward-connected).
#
# Honest boundary: file truth/quality = external data responsibility (grounding wall, #479);
# system does not judge, only seeds edges. Not verify_inverse (language antonym != algebraic inverse).
# This sample is dev/illustration only; production user supplies ConceptNet/WordNet export.

# adjective opposition (degree/temperature/size)
big small
long short
tall short
hot cold
light dark
deep shallow
thick thin
wide narrow

# direction / state opposition
up down
left right
front back
open close
alive dead
true false
win lose

# emotion / value opposition
love hate
good bad
beautiful ugly
reward punish
